  { number := 186, text := "4. Companion Lean SHALL encode the requirement and the honest residual as distinct facts. Companion Lean SHALL NOT treat emit equal to `ELF` as a proved identity." },
  { number := 187, text := "" },
  { number := 188, text := "### 4.7 Unassigned numbers and names with no assigned specification number" },
  { number := 189, text := "" },
  { number := 190, text := "1. fargo has no numbered specification and no assigned number. Authors SHALL NOT invent a numbered specification file for fargo in this effort." },
  { number := 191, text := "2. SSSP has no numbered specification file and no assigned number." },
  { number := 192, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol has no numbered specification file and no assigned number." },
  { number := 193, text := "4. Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. Legal Lean and Holy Lean remain named components without separate numbered specifications." },
  { number := 194, text := "5. Number 0009 is Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) (`0009_PDOSS.md`). Unlicense remains the license. The word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). Authors SHALL NOT assign 0009 to fargo or to Carbonado." },
  { number := 195, text := "6. A numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if that file is present. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept." },
  { number := 196, text := "7. Mentions of Vocabulary as a published specification 0009 do not conform. The catalog is CATE." },
  { number := 197, text := "" },
  { number := 198, text := "### 4.8 Form versus meaning" },
  { number := 199, text := "" },
  { number := 200, text := "1. Lean 4 SHALL be used to surface logical inconsistency in the models." },
  { number := 201, text := "2. Meaning proofs MUST NOT be treated as a second markdown form checker." },
  { number := 202, text := "3. `spec_check` remains the form checker." },
  { number := 203, text := "4. The named gate for this specifications repository remains the gate specified in `0007_CI.md`:" },
  { number := 204, text := "" },
  { number := 205, text := "```text" },
  { number := 206, text := "nix flake check \"path:$PWD\" --print-build-logs" },
  { number := 207, text := "```" },
  { number := 208, text := "" },
  { number := 209, text := "### 4.9 Sibling encodings for every published numbered specification" },
  { number := 210, text := "" },
  { number := 211, text := "1. Every published numbered markdown file at this repository root SHALL have a sibling Lean spec encoding `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` at that same root whose physical lines match that markdown, as specified in `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`." },
  { number := 212, text := "2. Proofs of those encodings SHALL live in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`." },
  { number := 213, text := "3. Mixing those encodings with their proofs in one file is nonconforming as specified in `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`. Companion Lean SHALL treat that mash as `False`." },
  { number := 214, text := "4. The Lean program `line_encodings_check` SHALL fail when a markdown line has no encoding or an encoding has no matching markdown line." },
  { number := 215, text := "5. `lean/Surmount.lean` SHALL require that every published numbered markdown file has that sibling encoding and that proofs are separate modules." },
  { number := 216, text := "" },
  { number := 217, text := "## 5. Conformance" },
  { number := 218, text := "" },
  { number := 219, text := "Work that claims this specification conforms if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 220, text := "" },
  { number := 221, text := "1. Numbered markdown is the contract humans read; the specification is also encoded in Lean; proofs live in separate Lean modules; theorem statements are not pasted into numbered markdown in this repository as a substitute for the composition proof (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 222, text := "2. Formal Vibefication citations keep the canonical Proof of Keags URLs; a numbered specification that names Keagan or Proof of Keags also contains the host `proofofkeags.com`; `spec_check` remains form and is not meaning (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 223, text := "3. This specifications repository keeps spec encodings distinct from proofs and from markdown form; Systems Lean product trees unify specification, proof, and implementation; that unification is not treated as a license to mix encodings with proofs here or to mix theorems into numbered markdown here; a mash of homes is treated as `False` (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 224, text := "4. The Lean module `Surmount` remains the single composition proof that reconciles the identities in Clause 4.4; a disagreement among models is treated as `False` (Clause 4.4)." },
  { number := 225, text := "5. beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are treated as ongoing and not ready for use, and are not described as never started or as ready (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 226, text := "6. Byte identity of Slake emit is treated as a product requirement and is not claimed true in this document (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 227, text := "7. fargo, SSSP, and Carbonado have no assigned specification numbers; Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; number 0009 is Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) and is not assigned to fargo or Carbonado; a numbered Vocabulary file does not exist; number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`); this document does not steal 0011 for fargo; number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 228, text := "8. Meaning proofs are not a second form checker; `spec_check` remains form; the named gate in `0007_CI.md` remains the gate for this repository (Clause 4.8)." },
  { number := 229, text := "9. Every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` whose physical lines match that markdown; proofs of those encodings live in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`; a mash of that sibling encoding with its proofs is treated as `False`; `line_encodings_check` fails on drift (Clause 4.9)." },
  { number := 230, text := "" },
  { number := 231, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming Surmount Systems product. Meeting these items is a claim about work that claims this specification, not about this markdown file as a shipped engine." },
  { number := 232, text := "" },
  { number := 233, text := "Optional recommendations (SHOULD, RECOMMENDED) do not break conformance when unmet, but authors SHOULD follow them unless there is a clear reason not to." },
  { number := 234, text := "" },
  { number := 235, text := "## 6. Residual" },
  { number := 236, text := "" },
  { number := 237, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, an unimplemented requirement, or an out of scope item named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. The repository root `RESIDUAL.md` restates residual for the numbered specification program; this clause is the residual record for this specification." },
  { number := 238, text := "" },
  { number := 239, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 240, text := "" },
  { number := 241, text := "1. fargo has no assigned specification number. This document does not create a numbered file for fargo. This document does not invent a number for fargo. This document does not steal 0005, 0006, 0007, 0008, 0009, 0010, 0011, 0012, 0013, or 0014 for fargo. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. Number 0013 is Lean Machine (`0013_Lean_Machine.md`). Number 0014 is Anunnaki Encoding (`0014_Anunnaki_Encoding.md`). Number 0015 stays unassigned. This document does not create a numbered file for 0015. `0003_beastdb.md` still names fargo as the interoperability path; that is a requirement on a future product, not a claim that fargo is specified or implemented." },
  { number := 242, text := "2. SSSP has no assigned specification number. This document does not create a numbered file for SSSP. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. This document MUST NOT be read as creating SSSP." },
  { number := 243, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Number 0005 is CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). Number 0006 is RSI (`0006_RSI.md`), not Carbonado. Number 0007 is Continuous Integration (`0007_CI.md`). Number 0008 is Formal Vibefication (`0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`). Number 0009 is Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) (`0009_PDOSS.md`). Unlicense remains the license. Number 0010 is this specification. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. Number 0013 is Lean Machine (`0013_Lean_Machine.md`). Number 0014 is Anunnaki Encoding (`0014_Anunnaki_Encoding.md`). Number 0015 is unassigned. This document does not steal 0015 for Carbonado. This document does not create a file for Carbonado." },
  { number := 244, text := "4. Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. That document is specification 0013. Legal Lean and Holy Lean remain named components without separate numbered specifications." },
  { number := 245, text := "5. Number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then Unlicense, and is now Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) by operator order. Unlicense remains the license. The word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). This document does not assign 0009 to fargo or to Carbonado. A numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if that file is present. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. Number 0013 is Lean Machine (`0013_Lean_Machine.md`). Number 0014 is Anunnaki Encoding (`0014_Anunnaki_Encoding.md`). Number 0015 is unassigned. This document MUST NOT steal number 0015." },
  { number := 246, text := "6. `SafeC` is part of specification 0002 ([0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 6.4 item 5) and is not a published specification number." },
  { number := 247, text := "" },
  { number := 248, text := "### 6.2 Product claims that are not ready for use" },
  { number := 249, text := "" },
  { number := 250, text := "1. This document specifies Surmount Systems stack composition. The products named here are ongoing and are not ready for use. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that those products never started or do not exist. Composition is not product readiness. Treating `stackIntegrates` as a claim that those products are ready for use is Cons False in `lean/Surmount.lean`. Theorem `mash_layers_inconsistent` already proves that a mash of homes is `False` and remains the catalog row. This document does not duplicate that theorem." },
  { number := 251, text := "2. Byte identity of Slake emit (Clause 3.4, Clause 4.6, and [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 6.3) is a requirement on a conforming Systems Lean and Slake product. This document does not claim that match already holds. The match is not claimed done. Slake work is ongoing and is not ready for use." },
  { number := 252, text := "3. The SSSSS and beastdb reality check named in `0007_CI.md` is a requirement on that stack. SSSSS and beastdb are ongoing and not ready for use. Do not write that they never started or do not exist. This document does not claim the check is done." },
  { number := 253, text := "4. `lean/Surmount.lean` is a composition of stack identities among human markdown, Lean spec encodings, Lean proofs, and product implementation. `0010_Surmount_Systems.lean` encodes the physical lines of this markdown file. `lean/Proofs_0010.lean` proves identities of that line encoding. Those modules are not a proof that Slake emit already matches `ELF`. They are not a proof that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, or Continuous Integration are ready for use. `stackIntegrates` remaining true is leftover depth of identities, not a shipped engine." },
  { number := 254, text := "5. Clause 4 states requirements on authors, agents, this specifications repository, and product trees that claim this specification. This document does not claim those requirements are already met by every session or every tree." },
  { number := 255, text := "" },
  { number := 256, text := "### 6.3 Pins this document does not add" },
  { number := 257, text := "" },
  { number := 258, text := "1. Lean 4, Idris 2, CompCert, and Rust are not pins of this specifications repository's `ref/`. `0002_Systems_Lean.md` places those Form 1 pins in the Systems Lean product tree. This repository MUST NOT copy those four trees into this repository's `ref/`." },
  { number := 259, text := "2. Formal Vibefication essays are cited by URL. They are not Clause 12 pins. This repository does not vendor those essays as Form 2 copies under `ref/`. Full license text is still not published on https://proofofkeags.com . Do not invent that license." },
  { number := 260, text := "3. ISO 24495-1:2023 and the US Federal Plain Language Guidelines remain informative prior art of CATE. They are not pins of this document." },
  { number := 261, text := "" },
  { number := 262, text := "### 6.4 Informative items this document names" },
  { number := 263, text := "" },
  { number := 264, text := "1. Formal Vibefication is named as the split used in this specifications repository. The research pages in Clause 2.2 are not Clause 12 pins of this document." },
  { number := 265, text := "2. CATE is specified in `0005_CATE.md`. CATE is not this specification." },
  { number := 266, text := "3. RSI is specified in `0006_RSI.md`. RSI is not this specification." },
  { number := 267, text := "4. Continuous Integration is specified in `0007_CI.md`. Continuous Integration is not this specification." },
  { number := 268, text := "5. Ahead of time emission is named in ordinary English. That phrasing is not a license to write leftover unstack." },
  { number := 269, text := "6. Companion models for CATE (`lean/CateSpec.lean` encodings, `lean/CateProofs.lean` theorems), RSI (`lean/RsiSpec.lean`, `lean/RsiProofs.lean`), Continuous Integration (`lean/CiSpec.lean`, `lean/CiProofs.lean`), beastdb (encodings and proofs under `lean/` for that product), SSSSS (`lean/SssssSpec.lean`, `lean/SssssProofs.lean`), Systems Lean (`lean/SystemsLeanSpec.lean`, `lean/SystemsLeanProofs.lean`), Formal Vibefication (`lean/FormalVibeficationSpec.lean`, `lean/FormalVibeficationProofs.lean`), Unlicense (`lean/UnlicenseSpec.lean`, `lean/UnlicenseProofs.lean`), Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`lean/TechTreeSpec.lean`, `lean/TechTreeProofs.lean`), Majestic Memex (`lean/MemexSpec.lean`, `lean/MemexProofs.lean`), Lean Machine (`lean/LeanMachineSpec.lean`, `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`), Anunnaki Encoding (`lean/AnunnakiSpec.lean`, `lean/AnunnakiProofs.lean`), and the CATE word catalog (`lean/VocabularySpec.lean`, `lean/VocabularyProofs.lean`) place encodings in Spec modules and theorems in Proofs modules. Collision tags in `lean/Vocabulary.lean` are encodings with proofs in `lean/VocabularyCollisionProofs.lean`. Mixing those in one mash is `False` under `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`. Sibling line encodings `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` and proof modules `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean` remain a separate split." },
