  { number := 275, text := "Current version line is 0.1.0 by operator order. Changelog history records that a 1.0.0 line existed. Residual Clause 6 records leftover depth that composition is not product readiness, that number 0014 is Anunnaki Encoding, and that number 0015 is unassigned." },
  { number := 276, text := "" },
  { number := 277, text := "### 1.0.0 - 20260825" },
  { number := 278, text := "" },
  { number := 279, text := "First publication of Surmount Systems as numbered specification 0010 with file name `0010_Surmount_Systems.md`. Records that this document is the human contract for how numbered specifications, Lean spec encodings, Lean proofs, and product paths fit. Records Formal Vibefication as specification 0008 with canonical Proof of Keags URLs and back linking. Records that numbered markdown is the contract humans read, that the specification is also encoded in Lean, that proofs live in separate Lean modules, and that Lean proofs are not the specification. Records that Systems Lean product trees unify specification, proof, and implementation and then Slake emits freestanding C ahead of time and MAY emit optional LLVM IR, and that this unification is not a license to mix encodings with proofs here or to mix theorems into numbered markdown here. Requires the Lean module `Surmount` as the single composition proof and requires Lean to treat a mash of identities as `False`. Requires residual honesty that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are ongoing and not ready for use. Requires byte identity of emit for a conforming Systems Lean and Slake product and records that the match is not claimed done." },
  { number := 280, text := "" },
  { number := 281, text := "This 1.0.0 also records: CATE is specification 0005; RSI is specification 0006; Continuous Integration is specification 0007; Formal Vibefication is specification 0008; Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) is specification 0009; Unlicense remains the license; the word catalog is owned by CATE as specification 0005; a numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist; number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`); this document does not steal 0011 for fargo; number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept; SSSSS is specification 0004; beastdb is specification 0003; Systems Lean is specification 0002; this specification is number 0010; fargo has no assigned specification number; SSSP has no assigned specification number; Carbonado has no assigned number; Lean Machine is specified as `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` whose physical lines match that markdown, with proofs in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`, checked by `line_encodings_check`; this document does not claim that a conforming Surmount Systems product exists." },
